  "id": "chunk_27",
  "chunk": "human players were included in the experimental setup, one would assume that\na human player of any skill level would not repeatedly reconsider actions that\nhave proved unsuccessful. The inability to learn from previous runs may relate\nto known LLM limitations in utilizing long contexts. Liu et al. [19] demon-\nstrated that LLMs struggle to use information in the middle of long contexts,\na phenomenon they term ‘lost in the middle.’ In ourZorkexperiments, rele-\nvant information about failed strategies from earlier in the conversation may be\neffectively invisible to the model when making decisions dozens of moves later.\nLet us turn to the ‘best’ performing LLM in our study: Claude Opus 4.5\nand take a closer look at the thinking-enabled version. As an illustration, the\nthought process by Claude shown in Example 1 seems reasonable at first glance.\n8\nExample 1\nGame output:This is part of a maze of twisty little passages, all alike.\nWhat command should I enter?",
